######## 56, 57. A new project can be read before its store section exists, and plain settings (shop)

$ kagebunshin project init shop
created project shop with environment dev

$ kagebunshin status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  file  local store  ok
project: shop
env: dev
0 keys
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  DATABASE_URL
  STRIPE_SECRET
  PORT
to fill in what is missing:
  you can run:
    kagebunshin project set-var shop dev PORT 3000
      (only if .env.example's value is the real setting, not a placeholder; a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
  ask the human:
    kagebunshin store set shop.dev DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET
      (it asks for the store passphrase, then each value)

$ kagebunshin diff
project: shop
env: dev
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  DATABASE_URL
  STRIPE_SECRET
  PORT
to fill in what is missing:
  you can run:
    kagebunshin project set-var shop dev PORT 3000
      (only if .env.example's value is the real setting, not a placeholder; a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
  ask the human:
    kagebunshin store set shop.dev DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET
      (it asks for the store passphrase, then each value)
kagebunshin: 3 keys in .env.example are not set by any source
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: warning: 3 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: DATABASE_URL, STRIPE_SECRET, PORT
MISSING DATABASE_URL
MISSING STRIPE_SECRET
MISSING PORT
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin next
project shop, environment dev: 0 of 3 keys set
next (you): set PORT as a plain setting to .env.example's value, only if that is the real setting and not a placeholder (a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
  kagebunshin project set-var shop dev PORT 3000
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please run `kagebunshin store set shop.dev DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET` in a terminal; it asks for the store passphrase, then each value. Or open the kagebunshin app (`kagebunshin app`) and say when it is open: I then run it, and you type the values in the app's window.

-- 57: a plain setting

$ kagebunshin project set-var shop dev PORT 3000
set PORT for environment dev of project shop

$ kagebunshin status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  file  local store  ok
project: shop
env: dev
1 key
  PORT  project file  = 3000
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  DATABASE_URL
  STRIPE_SECRET
to fill in what is missing:
  ask the human:
    kagebunshin store set shop.dev DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET
      (it asks for the store passphrase, then each value)
runs in the last day: 1, last at <time>

$ kagebunshin run --strict -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: 2 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: DATABASE_URL, STRIPE_SECRET
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin next
project shop, environment dev: 1 of 3 keys set
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please run `kagebunshin store set shop.dev DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET` in a terminal; it asks for the store passphrase, then each value. Or open the kagebunshin app (`kagebunshin app`) and say when it is open: I then run it, and you type the values in the app's window.
nothing more you can do until the human has done the above

-- 56 again: the human sets both secrets with one passphrase prompt

(human) $ kagebunshin store set shop.dev DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET
Passphrase for the local store: 
Value for DATABASE_URL: 
Value for STRIPE_SECRET: 
added

$ kagebunshin run --strict -- ./test.sh
ok   DATABASE_URL
ok   STRIPE_SECRET
ok   PORT

$ kagebunshin next
project shop, environment dev: done. 3 of 3 keys set; `./test.sh` ran with them on <day>. They come from file:shop.dev (2), the project file (1).

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo "port is $PORT, db is $DATABASE_URL"'
port is 3000, db is <redacted:DATABASE_URL>

-- a source wins over a plain setting

$ kagebunshin project set-var shop dev DATABASE_URL from-the-project-file
set DATABASE_URL for environment dev of project shop

$ kagebunshin status | grep -E 'DATABASE_URL|overrid'
  DATABASE_URL   file:shop.dev

$ kagebunshin project unset-var shop dev DATABASE_URL
removed DATABASE_URL from environment dev of project shop

-- known gap: a secret-looking name is accepted without a warning

$ kagebunshin project set-var shop dev API_TOKEN abc
set API_TOKEN for environment dev of project shop

$ kagebunshin project unset-var shop dev API_TOKEN
removed API_TOKEN from environment dev of project shop

$ cat $HOME/.config/kagebunshin/projects/shop.toml
schema = 1
remotes = ["github.com/acme/shop"]

[envs.dev]

[envs.dev.vars]
PORT = "3000"
